  "$comment": "languages-world-2 (11 November 2026): the WhatsApp allergen guard’s trigger words for URDU (ur-PK): الرجی / الرجک (and ایلرجی), عدم برداشت / برداشت نہیں, ہضم نہیں, حساسیت, سیلیک, گلوٹین فری / سے پاک, <allergen> کے بغیر / بغیر <allergen>, نہ ڈالیں / مت ڈالیں, نہیں کھا سکتا/سکتی, کے لیے محفوظ / موزوں, محفوظ ہے, شامل / موجود ہو سکتا, آلودگی, پرہیز — plus Roman Urdu (allergy hai, doodh ke baghair, nahi kha sakta). Written with the Urdu letters (ی ک ہ); zer/zabar/pesh and hamza fold away on both sides. Bare بغیر and bare سے پاک (inside سے پاکستان) are NOT stems, nor bare شامل نہیں (ڈلیوری شامل نہیں = delivery not included), nor bare مناسب (مناسب قیمت = fair price). OPTION B, as every other language: absence / safety words only, NOT the bare allergen names (a presence question may reach the AI, which answers only from the tags and gets the caveat). Matched with the Unicode normaliser. caveatWords: a tagged label of the codex allergen set (stored in English, lower case) → the words a reply may use for it (matched on the raw lower-cased reply, so written as the AI writes them). The country has no allergen set of its own yet, so caveatWords are for 'codex' (as MX, SG, HK, MY, TH and AE).",
